id: pm-9djr6d
title: Edit linked-test metadata in place with preserved provenance and atomic history
description: "Implement the complete GH1419 linked-test editor under the existing universal metadata reference lineage. Patch only explicit supported metadata fields; retain list position, immutable creation provenance and unchanged fields; stamp editor identity and time; reject empty or ambiguous selectors atomically; expose the same SDK operation through CLI and MCP."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-11T15:39:56.760Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-12T00:09:31.090Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-12T00:07:02.970Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-12T00:07:02.970Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: CLI and SDK edit one linked test by exact selector or one-based index; unchanged fields and original provenance survive; changed edit writes one field-level history event and editor metadata; equal retry preserves authoritative bytes; absent or ambiguous selectors refuse without mutation; invalid context patches are refused before persistence; command changes require fresh provenance/trust rather than preserving authorization; packed Node and Bun transports agree.
goal: project management = context management
parent: pm-gh1381
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Delivered SDK-first in-place metadata updates with explicit selectors and supported patches, preserved order and creation provenance, editor stamps, atomic history, byte-stable no-op retries, read-only/execution/mutation admission checks, sensitive-input and finish-preview telemetry protection, and paired MCP selector/patch dependencies."
expected_result: "SDK, CLI and MCP edits preserve metadata invariants, reject incompatible or incomplete requests, and pass unchanged repository quality and coverage gates."
actual_result: "14 integration cases, full 10,181-test suite and exact all-source 100/100/100/100 coverage pass; final focused 32 tests and 9 independent schema vectors pass. Typecheck and canonical static quality pass; schema and public declaration snapshots are regenerated and classified."
